---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<Layout
  title="Eworx SA — WordPress to Astro Case Study | rjp.digital"
  description="How I rebuilt Eworx SA's legacy WordPress site on Astro with Strapi and Splynx — giving the team content control and connecting customer enquiries directly to their ISP backend."
>
  <Header />

  <main>

    <!-- Back nav -->
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8 pt-8">
      <a href="/#work" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-ink-subtle)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)] transition-colors">
        <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M19 12H5M11 6l-6 6 6 6"/>
        </svg>
        Back to work
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Header -->
    <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 border-b border-[var(--color-border-light)]">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <div class="eyebrow mb-4">Case Study · 2025</div>
          <h1 class="text-5xl lg:text-6xl mb-6">Eworx SA</h1>
          <p class="text-xl text-[var(--color-ink-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-8">
            A South African ISP and managed IT provider with a WordPress site that had stopped working for their business — sparse content, a broken contact form, and no connection to the backend systems they rely on daily.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            {['Astro', 'Strapi', 'Splynx', 'Tailwind CSS'].map(tag => (
              <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-ink-muted)] px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-[var(--color-border)]">
                {tag}
              </span>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The problem -->
    <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 border-b border-[var(--color-border-light)]">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
          <div class="lg:col-span-4">
            <div class="eyebrow mb-4">The problem</div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl">A site that was losing them work.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="lg:col-span-7 lg:col-start-6 space-y-5 text-[var(--color-ink-muted)] leading-relaxed text-[17px]">
            <p>
              Eworx SA has been running managed IT and connectivity services for South African businesses since 1994. Their WordPress site wasn't keeping up. It had very little information on it — not enough for a prospect to understand what Eworx actually offers — and the contact form had a critical flaw: submissions weren't reliably reaching anyone.
            </p>
            <p>
              Potential customers were filling out the form and hearing nothing back. There was no way to know how many leads had slipped through. The site was also entirely dependent on a developer to update — any content change meant filing a request and waiting.
            </p>
            <p>
              The underlying issue wasn't cosmetic. It was structural: the site had no connection to the systems Eworx uses to run their business.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Before screenshot -->
    <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 border-b border-[var(--color-border-light)] bg-[var(--color-surface)]">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="eyebrow mb-6">Before</div>
        <figure>
          <img
            src="/images/work/eworx-before.png"
            alt="The old Eworx SA website — sparse layout, generic WordPress theme, minimal content"
            class="w-full rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] shadow-md"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-subtle)]">
            The old WordPress site — sparse content, no self-service, and a contact form that wasn't reliably delivering submissions.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What I built -->
    <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 border-b border-[var(--color-border-light)]">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
          <div class="lg:col-span-4">
            <div class="eyebrow mb-4">The solution</div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl">Connected to the systems that matter.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="lg:col-span-7 lg:col-start-6">
            <div class="space-y-8">

              <div class="flex gap-5">
                <div class="flex-none pt-1">
                  <span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)]">01</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">Astro frontend — fast and maintainable</h3>
                  <p class="text-[var(--color-ink-muted)] leading-relaxed">
                    The WordPress site was replaced with a custom Astro build. Static by default — sub-second loads, no plugin overhead, nothing that can silently break. The codebase is clean enough that a developer can pick it up without context.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="flex gap-5">
                <div class="flex-none pt-1">
                  <span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)]">02</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">Strapi CMS — content without a developer</h3>
                  <p class="text-[var(--color-ink-muted)] leading-relaxed">
                    Strapi sits behind the Astro frontend as the content layer. The Eworx team can now update service descriptions, add news, and manage the site's content through a clean admin UI — no code, no deployment pipeline, no waiting for a developer.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="flex gap-5">
                <div class="flex-none pt-1">
                  <span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)]">03</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">Splynx integration — enquiries become tickets</h3>
                  <p class="text-[var(--color-ink-muted)] leading-relaxed">
                    This was the key change. Eworx runs their ISP operations through Splynx — billing, support tickets, customer records. When a visitor submits a service enquiry or support request through the new site, it lands directly in Splynx as a ticket or lead. Nothing gets lost. No more form submissions disappearing into a void.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Outcome + CTA -->
    <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 border-b border-[var(--color-border-light)]">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-center">
          <div class="lg:col-span-7">
            <div class="eyebrow mb-4">The outcome</div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl mb-6">Live in 4 weeks. No leads lost.</h2>
            <p class="text-[var(--color-ink-muted)] leading-relaxed text-[17px] mb-6">
              From kick-off to launch in four weeks. The new site gives Eworx the content control they needed and closes the loop between website visitor and business system — so no enquiry goes unanswered again.
            </p>
            <a
              href="https://www.eworxsa.co.za/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="btn-secondary inline-flex items-center gap-2"
            >
              Visit the live site
              <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M7 17 L17 7 M9 7 L17 7 L17 15"/>
              </svg>
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="lg:col-span-4 lg:col-start-9">
            <dl class="space-y-6">
              <div class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)] pt-5">
                <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-ink-subtle)] mb-1">Delivery</dt>
                <dd class="text-2xl font-semibold">4 weeks</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)] pt-5">
                <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-ink-subtle)] mb-1">Stack</dt>
                <dd class="text-lg">Astro · Strapi · Splynx</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)] pt-5">
                <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-ink-subtle)] mb-1">Key result</dt>
                <dd class="text-lg">Enquiries route to Splynx — zero leads lost</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="py-16 lg:py-20">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="max-w-2xl">
          <h2 class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl mb-4">Have a similar problem?</h2>
          <p class="text-[var(--color-ink-muted)] leading-relaxed text-[17px] mb-8">
            If your site is losing leads, hard to update, or disconnected from the tools your business runs on — that's exactly the kind of thing I fix. Get in touch for an honest conversation about what's possible.
          </p>
          <a href="/#contact" class="btn-primary">
            Start a conversation
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/>
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
